From 9a99972ad66fa27051f47464a198ce9f1ffcc973 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fred <fred@home>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:08:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nav): initialize/clear CNavArea open-list state (hostage
 AI crash)

Crash signature (symbolized with the exact server cs.so,
build id ad2ea84fd6b8d77372ad9bee66e605c8a5f7708e,
ReGameDLL 5.30.0.830-dev, commit b088984):

  SIGSEGV in CNavArea::UpdateOnOpenList()
  CHostage::PreThink -> CHostage::IdleThink
    -> CHostageImprov::OnUpdate -> HostageIdleState::OnUpdate
    -> CHostageImprov::IsTerroristNearby
    -> CHostageImprov::GetClosestPlayerByTravelDistance
    -> NavAreaBuildPath<ShortestPathCost>
    -> CNavArea::UpdateOnOpenList

Recurring on the same build (not a one-off):
  - 2026-10-03: cs.so+0x20133a, this->m_prevOpen = 0x73252220
  - 2026-11-02: cs.so+0x201376, other->m_prevOpen = 1 (write to 0x1b9)

Live map at crash: cs_mansion09_mod_br (cs_ hostage map with 3
hostage_entity), hostage_ai_enable 1, no bots, prometheus.amxx not
loaded, no .ent override / sv_use_entity_file.

Not the map's nav file: cs_mansion09_mod_br.nav is valid (v5, 535
areas, unique IDs, valid connections, max m_approachCount = 16,
parses to EOF, saved BSP size matches).

Root cause: the A* pathfinder keeps nav areas on a linked "open list",
and each area stores whether it is on that list (m_openMarker) plus its
list neighbours (m_nextOpen / m_prevOpen). In plain terms, the
pathfinder could think an area was on the list when it was not, then
follow a garbage link.

  - CNavArea::Initialize() never initialized m_nextOpen / m_prevOpen /
    m_openMarker, so a newly created or loaded area contained leftover
    heap data. IsOpen() could return true for an area that was never
    added, and UpdateOnOpenList() would follow a bogus m_prevOpen and
    read/write invalid memory.
  - An area destroyed while still linked was not removed from the list,
    so the list could keep a pointer to freed memory.

Fix:
  - initialize m_nextOpen/m_prevOpen/m_openMarker in Initialize()
  - unlink from the open list in ~CNavArea()
  - clear the static open list in DestroyNavigationMap()
  - guard UpdateOnOpenList() with IsOpen()
---
 regamedll/game_shared/bot/nav_area.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/regamedll/game_shared/bot/nav_area.cpp b/regamedll/game_shared/bot/nav_area.cpp
index 845b2a3fd..44f0e0635 100644
--- a/regamedll/game_shared/bot/nav_area.cpp
+++ b/regamedll/game_shared/bot/nav_area.cpp
@@ -173,6 +173,10 @@ void CNavArea::Initialize()
 
 	m_prevHash = nullptr;
 	m_nextHash = nullptr;
+
+	m_nextOpen = nullptr;
+	m_prevOpen = nullptr;
+	m_openMarker = 0;
 }
 
 // Constructor used during normal runtime
@@ -261,6 +265,10 @@ CNavArea::CNavArea(CNavNode *nwNode, class CNavNode *neNode, class CNavNode *seN
 // Destructor
 CNavArea::~CNavArea()
 {
+	// detach from the A* open list before the memory is freed
+	if (IsOpen())
+		RemoveFromOpenList();
+
 	// tell all bots that this area no longer exists
 	TheCSBots()->OnDestroyNavDataNotify(NAV_NOTIFY_DESTROY_AREA, this);
 
@@ -918,6 +926,9 @@ void DestroyNavigationMap()
 {
 	CNavArea::m_isReset = true;
 
+	// the open list may still reference areas that are about to be deleted
+	CNavArea::ClearSearchLists();
+
 	// destroy all hiding spots
 	DestroyHidingSpots();
 
@@ -2493,6 +2504,10 @@ void CNavArea::AddToOpenList()
 // TODO: "bubbling" does unnecessary work, since the order of all other nodes will be unchanged - only this node is altered
 void CNavArea::UpdateOnOpenList()
 {
+	// only valid if this area is actually on the open list
+	if (!IsOpen())
+		return;
+
 	// since value can only decrease, bubble this area up from current spot
 	while (m_prevOpen && this->GetTotalCost() < m_prevOpen->GetTotalCost())
 	{
